WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:55.540
...still emphasizing the distinctiveness of each person in relation. I don't

00:00:55.540 --> 00:01:00.140
see such a strong problem with emphasizing individual choice,

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:07.140
rather I see the encouragement and the ideal as being one that's always being one that's choosing to do the best for the other.

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:13.530
I think that has more to do with the

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:18.390
transcending objective nature of human goods. I mean

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:19.770
it does have to do with humanity,

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:22.020
but I can understand how

00:01:24.729 --> 00:01:29.580
theologically one can still affirm certain rights as...

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:33.330
I haven't read the book, but I know he has
written on this...

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:35.650
and trinitarian community.

00:01:40.009 --> 00:01:43.490
In the perspective that I'm putting forward

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:45.940
human freedom is

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:47.000
the mode

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.930
in which we practice faith

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:50.680
in the goods

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:56.140
that God gives us, whether these goods be
human relationships or the divine

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:58.070
human relationship itself.

00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:01.440
Whether these goods be material or spiritual

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:06.330
or relate to the non-human creation.

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:07.479
That

00:02:07.479 --> 00:02:08.750
when one then

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:10.299
attaches right

00:02:10.299 --> 00:02:12.069
to freedom,

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:18.700
again I come back to this sort of misplacement.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:20.040
One is

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:23.810
singling out the mode of participation as
something

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:26.329
having a kind of

00:02:26.329 --> 00:02:28.420
priority in the circumstance,

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:38.799
an independent conceptual

00:02:38.799 --> 00:02:41.989
moral focus.

00:02:41.989 --> 00:02:43.209
And that

00:02:43.209 --> 00:02:44.809
I'm not going to do.

00:02:44.809 --> 00:02:46.829
And if I differ from him 

00:02:46.829 --> 00:02:50.959
it would probably be on that point

00:02:50.959 --> 00:02:53.450
rather than

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.859
necessarily the relational one.

00:02:56.859 --> 00:02:58.739
But I do think

00:03:07.529 --> 00:03:11.409
my point about judicalizing human relations

00:03:11.409 --> 00:03:13.529
that I think happens with…

00:03:14.929 --> 00:03:20.119
even when people are not oriented to demanding
their own rights, they're demanding rights

00:03:20.119 --> 00:03:22.129
of their neighbors.

00:03:22.129 --> 00:03:27.619
That still to me as a theologian smacks of
judicalizing human relationships.

00:03:27.619 --> 00:03:28.839
It's what the

00:03:28.839 --> 00:03:33.580
reformers, both

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.299
continental and English would call...

